This really fuckin' sucks.
My cursed bag of holding was eating my stuff, so I went to take all the crap 
out.  Suddenly, the dreaded message "Segmentation fault" pops up right in the
middle of the screen -- it doesn't even clear.  No surprise to me that the
save file is non-existent.  [I would've rather faced a Snake, floating eye,
gremlin, giant mimic, freezing sphere, water nymph, trapper, giant beetle,
trapper,tengu,orc captain, and mountain nymph all at once than face total
annihilation, lemme tell ya.]

Man, I had just finished the mage quest, which was especially annoying because
I couldn't see invisible . . .  I had MagicBane plus my trusty +4 athame
and crysknife, I had reduced my AC by three points by throwing gold at 
priestesses, I had lots of identified gems, gauntlets of power, a couple
of genocide scrolls to spare . . .  in short a good character with good
stuff, intrinsics, discoveries, etc (well, lots of good stuff before the
evil villain cursed about 1/3 of it!)  Why is nethack so cruel??

It seems that NH has problems with dropping stuff in vortexes, polymorhping 
and dropping stuff, and now taking objects out of containers.  Sigh . . .
Yes, we still have version 3.1, and no, I don't think the U. C. SysAdmin
people are particularly interested in keeping up with the patches.

